    "### Model specification\n",
    "\n",
    "`log(SalePrice) ~ Normal(alpha + X beta + neighborhood effect, sigma)`\n",
    "\n",
    "The baseline uses the shared intercept and three standardized predictors. The expanded model adds four standardized predictors and a neighborhood intercept.\n",
    "\n",
    "Priors:\n",
    "- Shared intercept: Normal(training mean log price, 0.7).\n",
    "- Standardized predictor coefficients: Normal(0, 0.5).\n",
    "- Residual standard deviation: HalfNormal(0.5).\n",
    "- Neighborhood scale: HalfNormal(0.3).\n",
    "- Standardized neighborhood effects: zero-sum Normal with scale 1.\n",
    "\n",
    "Sampling: four chains; 1,500 tuning steps and 1,000 retained draws per chain; target acceptance 0.95. Diagnostics report R-hat, effective sample sizes, and divergences. The sampling check uses R-hat < 1.01, bulk and tail ESS >= 400, and zero divergences.\n"
   ]
